[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Bounded MOS LEVEL=1 semiconductor profile

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-MOS1-CURRENT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit bounded Shichman-Hodges channel
STATEMENT: >>>
The native engine shall evaluate MOS LEVEL=1 cutoff, linear and saturation drain-to-source current with source/drain reversal, NMOS/PMOS polarity, threshold, effective beta, GAMMA/PHI body effect and LAMBDA channel-length modulation. Effective parameters and all terminals shall be validated. With nonzero GAMMA, positive effective body bias shall explicitly refuse until the forward continuation is qualified. The generated model shall require positive effective L and W as resolved by SEMI-MOS1-GEOMETRY-001, and shall refuse unsupported model levels, parameters, temperature and geometry rather than silently omit their effects.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/mos1.rs, circuit/compile/Newton, Mos1Preparation. Verification: tests/mos1_channel.rs analytical currents, modes, polarity, malformed values and seeded properties; Mos1Tests and actual typed-client Mos1NativeOracleIntegration. This is a bounded model profile, not general LEVEL=1 compatibility.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-MOS1-GEOMETRY-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Independent level-one MOS geometry defaults
STATEMENT: >>>
For bounded LEVEL=1 NMOS and PMOS, the frontend shall resolve L and W independently. An explicit instance dimension overrides the model dimension, which overrides the default 100 micrometres. Named values shall evaluate in their declaring scopes. The effective geometry shall feed channel strength and the supported overlap capacitors. Duplicates within one card and nonpositive effective dimensions shall refuse circuit preparation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: Mos1Preparation. Verification: Mos1Tests.Geometry_defaults_resolve_independently and Invalid_instance_geometry_refuses_atomically. Instrumented ngspice-47+ OP on the original MOS1_out model and instances returns (L,W) of (3,9), (5,10), and (100,100) micrometres respectively. This evidence measures parameter precedence separately from requested nested-DC analysis and waveform comparison.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-MOS1-JACOBIAN-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Four-terminal channel derivatives
STATEMENT: >>>
The MOS channel shall supply analytic drain, gate, source and bulk derivatives to DC Newton and complex AC. Derivatives shall conserve terminal current and common-mode invariance and shall be checked against independent finite differences in all supported regions and polarities. Channel observables shall exclude explicitly composed displacement current; generated outer drain senses shall expose total drain current.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: Mos1Model::linearize, newton channel stamping, API i_channel; existing branch i(M) mapping. Verification: deterministic and seeded 128-case derivative properties and independent ngspice complex AC voltage/current comparisons. Independent AC physical audit remains NotChecked when bias is unavailable.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-MOS1-BODY-Q-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Physical MOS body-junction storage
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated bounded MOS1 model shall compose signed bulk-drain and bulk-source junction conduction and genuine nonlinear depletion storage using IS, CBD/CBS, PB, MJ and FC at TNOM=27. Backward Euler shall use accepted Q history and AC shall use the full nonlinear derivative. Shorted body-junction terminals may be omitted because their differential voltage, net current and charge contribution are identically zero. Nonlinear stored-energy qualification shall remain explicit NotChecked.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Reuse: qualified SpiceDiodeModel Q and existing accepted-step history. Verification: generated independent native reference circuits include nonzero CBD/CBS and nonzero source impedance, both polarities/providers, DC/AC/BE.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-MOS1-OVERLAP-Q-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Gate overlap storage without false intrinsic parity
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated bounded MOS1 model shall stamp gate-source CGSO times W, gate-drain CGDO times W and gate-bulk CGBO times L as explicit overlap capacitances. Derived capacitances shall be finite and preserve nonzero input terms. The separate intrinsic TOX mapping is specified in SEMI-MOS1-TOX-001. Overlap capacitance shall never be described as intrinsic or complete MOS gate-charge parity.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Source evidence: exact SpiceSharp 3.2.3 model/common parameters and dynamic behavior, and ngspice mos1temp.c disabling oxideCapFactor when TOX absent or zero. Verification: typed binder and nonzero-overlap complex AC/BE native oracle. Area/sidewall junction terms and higher MOS levels remain outside this profile.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-MOS1-SERIES-R-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit MOS1 terminal resistance
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded MOS1 profile shall stamp nonnegative model RD and RS in ohms between the corresponding external and intrinsic terminals. Zero shall preserve the original node allocation. The channel, body junctions and overlap capacitance shall attach to the intrinsic terminals, and the drain observable shall retain total external current. A positive resistance with unrepresentable conductance shall refuse.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification uses Mos1Tests and compat/ngspice/mos1-series-resistance.cir. Sheet-resistance geometry and other MOS levels remain outside this profile.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-BSIM330-SELECT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Exact BSIM3 selector and unsupported-kernel diagnostic
STATEMENT: >>>
A model VERSION assignment using a contiguous three-part dotted number shall retain its full physical source range and value. Explicit NMOS and PMOS LEVEL 8 or 49 with VERSION 3.3.0 shall identify the exact model. If that kernel is unavailable, preparation shall refuse before publishing an operation plan. It shall neither select MOS1 nor accept a different BSIM version as 3.3.0.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: generated modelVersionAssignment, DeclarationExtraction, Mos1Preparation and CircuitReadiness. Verification: Mos1Tests and the BSIM330 admission replay. Native DC/AC/transient support is a separate contract.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-MOS1-MEYER-001
TITLE: Effective intrinsic MOS1 displacement
STATEMENT: >>>
The native MOS1 channel primitive shall accept a finite nonnegative effective oxide capacitance in farads, defaulting to zero. AC shall stamp the three incremental Meyer gate branches at the solved bias. Backward Euler shall use the mean of trial and previously accepted branch capacitances times the branch voltage increment divided by the step, with equal and opposite terminal currents.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The classic Meyer partition follows the Berkeley/ngspice convention, cross-checked against the local pinned RSpice source in classic/capacitance.rs. It is a branch displacement law, not a globally integrable terminal charge or energy model. Verification uses mos1_channel and the SchematicLab mos1-meyer ngspice fixture. Generated TOX binding is specified in SEMI-MOS1-TOX-001.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-MOS1-TOX-001
TITLE: Derive intrinsic MOS1 capacitance from TOX
STATEMENT: >>>
For a positive TOX in metres, the generated LEVEL=1 profile shall set the native effective oxide capacitance to (3.9 × 8.854214871e-12 / TOX) × W × L in farads, using the resolved instance and model geometry. Where KP is omitted it shall use the ngspice default mobility of 600 cm²/V/s with that oxide capacitance per area. Explicit KP shall take precedence. Absent or zero TOX shall omit intrinsic oxide capacitance and preserve the previous KP default. Negative TOX or a nonrepresentable derived capacitance shall refuse before producing a native request.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: Mos1Preparation and the native oxide_farads wire field. Effective geometry follows SEMI-MOS1-GEOMETRY-001. Geometry corrections such as LD and user-supplied UO remain outside the profile. Verification: Mos1Tests and Mos1NativeOracleIntegration on both CPU providers.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-JFET1-SQUARE-LAW-001
TITLE: Lower the bounded level-1 JFET channel
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated frontend shall lower three-terminal NJF and PJF level-1 cards with the default B=1 law. It shall convert JFET BETA to the shared square-law convention, orient both gate junctions by polarity, and stamp RD and RS outside the intrinsic terminals. The drain sensor shall retain the external drain current. Invalid values and unsupported model or instance parameters shall refuse preparation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification uses JfetTests and the original jfet/jfet_vds-vgs.cir operating point and nested DC sweep. This profile covers LEVEL, VTO, BETA, LAMBDA, RD, RS and IS at nominal temperature. Charge, alternative B, and temperature laws are separate.
<<<
